"1. The Attorney General is authorized and directed, in the name of the United States or otherwise permitted by law, to coordinate, conduct, initiate, maintain or defend:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Litigation before the Emergency Court of Appeals for and on behalf of the Secretary of Agriculture, the Secretary of Commerce, and the Reconstruction Finance Corporation, respectively;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 1(a)","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Litigation against violators of regulations, schedules or orders relating to maximum prices pertaining to any commodity which has been removed from price control;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 1(b)","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Litigation arising out of Directive 41, as amended, of the Office of Economic Stabilization pertaining to the withholding of subsidies because of noncompliance with or violations of control orders.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 1(c)","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"2. Nothing herein shall be deemed to restrict or limit the powers conferred upon the Attorney General by law with respect to the conduct, settlement, disposition or review of litigation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 2","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"3. The functions and duties of the Attorney General under this order shall be performed by him, or subject to his direction and control, by such officers or agencies of the Department of Justice as he may designate, and there shall be made available to the Attorney General, pursuant to the provisions of Executive Order No. 9784 of September 25, 1946, any files or records pertinent to the subject matter hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 3","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"4. This order shall become effective June 1, 1947.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); para. 4","sha256":"5f343f9623b5ff192b1d1b6c00f094013b95221eb7a6605b04c1fd9f33f6f5a4","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9842-conduct-certain-litigation-arising-under-wartime-legislation"},"scope_id":"EO:9842#para4","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"12 FR 2646, PDF pages 4-4","sha256":"8257365d7d3d1ab12510a0f347b3a389d84d1eadc7e5096f788de93eda8143da","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1947-04-25/pdf/FR-1947-04-25.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 8 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:9842"}
